Obviously, specimens S1 and S2 exhibit minimal corrosion; both show only slight surface attack. By contrast, S3 (the Cu-bearing variant) displays pronounced corrosion with clearly visible residues of corrosion products. The specimens after the corrosion test are shown in Figure  9 , both as cast and post heat treatment. A key factor is that Cu is solved in the  α \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
